independent summary projections, ten summary tokens, identities, two interaction blocks, four task tokens, raw/count skip and four towers',\n      'Identical parameter shapes, module declaration/initialization order and forward operation shapes across the four new arms']\ncontrasts=[]\nfor control,intervention,confounds,yes,no in [\n ('normalized_pair','Replace only bank 2 normalized summary u with count-scaled summary n*u/2 (split).',\n  ['Count multiplication changes input and gradient scale; explicit counts already allow either arm to approximate the other.', 'Single fixed seed cannot establish robustness; extra direct skip and token path are not separately identified.'],\n  'If split improves click over normalized_pair while preserving its auxiliary performance, provisionally support access to both scales; compare all other controls and plan paired repetitions.',\n  'If matched normalized duplication equals split, do not credit the scaled view; any improvement over the old parent may be added capacity.'),\n ('scaled_pair','Replace only bank 1 count-scaled summary with normalized content (split).',\n  ['The intervention changes conditioning and gradient magnitudes as well as content scale.', 'Same seed gives a matched initialization, not independent mechanistic replication.'],\n  'If split recovers auxiliary quality without a material click reduction, retain the complementary-scale hypothesis provisionally.',\n  'If scaled_pair dominates, abandon a joint-benefit claim for this implementation and examine a simpler scaled representation.'),\n ('fused_pair','Keep normalized and count-scaled content in distinct banks rather than averaging them before both projections.',\n  ['Early fusion changes the input scale; counts remain available, so this tests finite-recipe inductive bias rather than extra information.', 'No causal inference about original DIN or external unified methods follows.'],\n  'Only split beating the fused replacement supports keeping the two scales separately addressable in this architecture.',\n  'A fused tie or win rejects evidence for separate-bank organization; do not relabel it as support just because both beat a parent.')]:\n contrasts.append(dict(parent_ref='g0-r0001-mass_normalized',intervention=intervention,control=control,held_fixed=held,remaining_confounds=confounds,decision_if_supported=yes,decision_if_not_supported=no))\ncontrasts.append(dict(parent_ref='g0-r0001-mass_normalized',intervention='Compare new normalized_pair and scaled_pair to the recorded single-bank normalized and count-scaled ancestors; compare split to baseline-din for selection.',control='g0-r0001-mass_normalized; g0-r0001-count_scaled; baseline-din',held_fixed=held[:2],remaining_confounds=['New bank/projection/readout width changes capacity and random draw alignment against ancestors; these are predictive and cost references, not pure mechanism contrasts.', 'All historical results are single-seed validation; no bootstrap predictions are available in this phase.'],decision_if_supported='Distinguish added capacity from representation effects using the three within-suite replacements; only validation click AUC can replace baseline-din as incumbent.',decision_if_not_supported='Retain baseline-din and report null/negative results; no improvement or mechanism success is assumed.'))\nobservations=[]\nfor t in trials:\n v=t['validation']; per=v['per_task']; aux=sum(per[k]['auc'] for k in ['cart','fav','buy'])/3\n observations.append(dict(trial_id=t['id'],status=t['status'],click_auc=v['auc'],click_logloss=v['logloss'],auxiliary_mean_auc=aux,wall_seconds=t['wall_seconds'],parameters=t['parameters'],error=t.get('error')))\nstudy=dict(\n id='g0-r0002-paired-content-volume-tokens',protocol_ref=p_hash,\n evidence_refs=[t['id'] for t in trials],\n question='Under the single-pass frozen protocol, can separate normalized-content and count-scaled-content summary tokens reduce the observed click/auxiliary tradeoff relative to equal-capacity duplicate or early-fused summaries?',\n hypothesis='The same shared summary scale is an optimization bottleneck: normalized summaries favor auxiliary tasks while exposure-count scaling favors click under this recipe. Providing both views in distinct independently projected banks may let task prediction retain complementary scales. This adds no sample information: the parent already exposes log counts and all views are deterministic functions of the same authorized content. Proposed mechanism is a representation/conditioning bias, not evidence that learned activation intensity is necessary.',\n nearest_work=[\n dict(source_ref='paper:din',verification='read',difference='Archived primary v4 section4.3 lines271-277 already motivates unnormalized activation intensity. This proposal uses the inherited normalized per-field sigmoid retrieval, deterministic visible-count scaling and paired post-pooling tokens, rather than DIN event-level scalar local activation. Neither intensity preservation nor original novelty is claimed.'),\n dict(source_ref='unirank-code:HiFormer',verification='implementation_checked',difference='Pinned benchmark forward113-159 pools events then uses field/task tokens and heterogeneous interaction blocks. We inherit only the broad stacked pattern from the local ancestor and use paired summary-scale banks, shared small attention blocks and direct summary/static skips. Original paper text is unavailable through the authorized reader; no equivalence or priority claim.'),\n dict(source_ref='unirank-code:TokenMixer',verification='implementation_checked',difference='Pinned benchmark forward112-158 uses global/group tokenizers after target pooling, reversible token mixing and mean readout. Proposed banks organize two scales of the same five inherited summaries; there is no reversible transport, global/chunk tokenizer or mean-token readout. Original full paper is unavailable; novelty remains unverified.'),\n dict(source_ref='paper:dmr',verification='read',difference='Only author README is available; it warns its behavior data has category/brand/type but no item IDs. Current histories are previous ad exposures under the frozen adapter. No original DMR mechanism or numerical result is imported.')],\n inherited_components=['g0-r0001-mass_normalized complete normalized field-retrieval and downstream interaction backbone; verified source hash ecb9698efa49ce67c7df576df98a4b77de5a87db6a6cba881ea3505cfeffd116', 'Shared field embeddings; target/context queries; sigmoid normalization; global exposure retrieval; historical action values; five feedback presence/count features; static projections; two shared attention/FFN blocks; four task tokens and Dice towers; raw static/summary/count skip; default host loss', 'g0-r0001-count_scaled deterministic exposure count/2 scale, applied after normalized retrieval for a second view; not learned activation mass'],\n proposed_difference='Replace the single five-token history-summary bank with two independently projected five-token banks. Candidate feeds (u,n*u/2); equal-capacity replacements feed (u,u), (n*u/2,n*u/2), or (f,f) with f=(u+n*u/2)/2. All arms retain pre-existing explicit group log counts and absence gates in both banks and the direct readout. n is exposure count, not individual feedback count. Task tokens and towers can combine either bank; a positive result cannot on its own locate the benefit in token interaction versus the raw summary skip.',\n predictions=[\n 'Primary selection stays full-population validation click AUC; baseline-din remains incumbent at 0.6555440824200336 until a measured candidate exceeds it. All four AUC/logloss, auxiliary mean, parameter counts and measured cost must be reported even when primary fails.',\n 'Predeclared practical joint-benefit target: split improves click AUC by at least 0.002 over normalized_pair, stays within 0.001 click AUC of scaled_pair, and stays within 0.003 auxiliary mean AUC of normalized_pair while exceeding scaled_pair auxiliary mean by at least 0.003. These are screening margins, not significance thresholds.',\n 'Separate-bank evidence additionally requires split to exceed fused_pair in at least one task objective without violating the above click/auxiliary guardrails. A tie gives no separate-token mechanism support.',\n 'Evaluate paired differences within the existing bins empty,1-16,17-64,>64 histories, with sample/positive/negative counts. Prior normalized versus scaled differences are largest within short nonempty click histories; this is a preregistered follow-up prompted by exploratory historical slices. No empty-history direct-content benefit is expected; trained global parameters can still change its predictions.'\n ],\n falsifiers=[\n 'If normalized_pair or scaled_pair matches/dominates split, the complementary-scale representation claim lacks support even if split beats a historical parent.',\n 'If fused_pair matches/dominates split, separate addressability is unsupported; report it as null or negative for the tested organization.',\n 'Click improvement coupled to auxiliary deterioration comparable to scaled_pair fails the predicted tradeoff relief. Auxiliary improvement alone cannot select a new incumbent.',\n 'NaNs, invalid masks, dependence on invisible padded item values, missing outputs or excessive runtime are implementation failures, not mechanism refutations. Retain receipts/costs and distinguish these from valid predictive failures.',\n 'A single successful seed is provisional; changed-seed reversal weakens the finding. No result establishes learned-gate intensity or temporal ordering mechanisms.'\n ],\n alternative_explanations=['Observed historical scale differences could reflect count/prevalence or optimizer conditioning, not useful target-dependent intensity; mass_sum and count_scaled differ in click AUC by only 0.0000177175.', 'Extra projections, larger tower inputs and five additional tokens may explain gains over single-bank ancestors; new duplicate replacements match these additions exactly.', 'Normalized/scaled signals are recoverable from each other using the already available counts, so gains would be finite-capacity/training effects rather than information gains.', 'Post-interaction task tokens and direct summary skips both carry the changed representation. The suite cannot prove task routing, attention use, multi-task gradient conflict, or a temporal sequence mechanism.', 'All outcomes inherit released static snapshots, whole-window filtering/vocabulary and official_offline feedback; point-in-time production effectiveness is unestablished.', 'One seed, adaptive trajectory choice and aggregate AUC can hide user-cluster variation. Current coding jail provides no raw data, trained checkpoints or paired predictions for additional diagnostics.'],\n contrasts=contrasts,\n cost_plan=dict(estimate_ref='baseline-din; g0-r0000-field_feedback; g0-r0000-event_feedback; g0-r0000-field_global; g0-r0000-event_global; g0-r0001-mass_sum; g0-r0001-mass_normalized; g0-r0001-count_scaled; g0-r0001-softmax_reference; run://r-001 protocol estimated_unit_seconds=481.3475877419114 and trial_cap_seconds=1203.3689693547785',all_variants_counted=True,\n attribution_reserve='Four host variants count, including controls and any failed attempts. Historical jobs cost 316.99-328.91s each, but token/readout expansion is unmeasured; plan roughly 600s each (2400s), conservatively up to four unchanged caps=4813.48s. Additional preparation/checks consume wall-clock budget. Reserve at least 10000s for three paired seeds of split and its closest two controls if a consequential result appears, plus 5000s for discriminating failure/attribution checks; no automatic repeats in this proposal. All four variants use one retrieval and matched shapes; for six item fields, analytic extra trainable count is 85696 over the parent, pending host verification. Measured equal-compute comparison is deferred, and this is a matched data-pass study only.',\n assessment_reserve='Ke